    "title": "LESSON 11: REFLEXIVE VERBS",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "REFLEXIVE VERBS — the action comes",
          "back to the subject. Add a",
          "reflexive pronoun before the verb:",
          "",
          "se lever (to get up):                Press 1",
          "je me lève       tu te lèves",
          "il/elle se lève",
          "nous nous levons",
          "vous vous levez",
          "elles se lèvent",
          "",
          "Notice the pronoun MATCHES the",
          "subject: je↔me, tu↔te, il/on↔se,",
          "nous↔nous, vous↔vous, ils↔se.",
          "",
          "Before a vowel, me/te/se elide:      Press 2",
          "s'habiller, s'appeler, s'endormir."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Leçon onze",
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Je me lève. Tu te lèves. Il se lève. Nous nous levons. Vous vous levez. Elles se lèvent.",
          "2": "S'habiller. S'appeler. S'endormir."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "REFLEXIVES IN THE PAST — always use",
          "être, no exceptions. Genuinely",
          "easier than the avoir/être split",
          "you'll meet next for other verbs:",
          "",
          "je me suis levé(e)                   Press 1",
          "(I got up)",
          "elle s'est habillée                  Press 2",
          "(she got dressed)",
          "",
          "The past participle AGREES with the",
          "subject, like an adjective — add -e",
          "for feminine (levée, habillée), -s",
          "for plural, -es for feminine plural."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "je me suis levé",
          "2": "elle s'est habillée"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
